  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-ui-scrollblock (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package fingerprints the OS/architecture and downloads a second-stage binary from a rotating list of Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, path /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe). If the download fails it falls back to a DNS-TXT exfiltration channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the Windows temp dir), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via cmd.exe /c start /b or /bin/sh -c '... \u0026'. This is a remote binary download-and-execute dropper that runs automatically when the module is loaded.",
